---
const problems = [
	{
		title: 'Observation is unscheduled',
		body: 'Absurdity arrives on its own timeline. Your sharpest commentary currently depends on the right person happening to be in the meeting where it happens.',
	},
	{
		title: 'Wit is a single point of failure',
		body: 'Most organizations concentrate their entire satirical capacity in one individual. When that person leaves, the jokes leave with them. This is key-person risk.',
	},
	{
		title: 'Grievances are an unmanaged asset',
		body: 'Your teams produce high-quality frustration daily. It depreciates in Slack threads — unstructured, unprocessed, and entirely unmonetized.',
	},
];
---

<section class="border-b border-line">
	<div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-5 py-20 sm:px-8 sm:py-28">
		<div class="max-w-2xl" data-reveal>
			<p class="font-mono text-[11px] font-medium tracking-[0.22em] text-accent uppercase">The problem</p>
			<h2 class="mt-4 text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-balance sm:text-4xl">
				Noticing things doesn’t <span class="accent-word">scale</span>.
			</h2>
			<p class="mt-5 text-lg leading-relaxed text-muted">
				Organizations generate dysfunction continuously, at every level, in every meeting. Commentary
				production has not kept pace. Satire remains artisanal: unstructured, unrepeatable, and
				dependent on someone being funny at the exact moment it matters.
			</p>
		</div>

		<div class="mt-14 grid gap-10 sm:grid-cols-3 sm:gap-8" data-reveal>
			{problems.map((problem, i) => (
				<div class="border-t border-line pt-6">
					<p class="font-mono text-xs text-faint">0{i + 1}</p>
					<h3 class="mt-3 text-base font-semibold tracking-tight">{problem.title}</h3>
					<p class="mt-2.5 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-muted">{problem.body}</p>
				</div>
			))}
		</div>

		<p class="mt-16 max-w-2xl text-2xl leading-snug font-semibold tracking-tight text-balance sm:text-3xl" data-reveal>
			Satire is a pipeline problem.<br />
			<span class="text-muted">The category was hiding in plain sight.</span>
		</p>
	</div>
</section>
